data: {"text": " MDM2/MDM4 antagonists (e.g., idasanutlin, navtemadlin) require "}

data: {"text": "wild-type"}

data: {"text": " p53 and are ineffective in TP53-mutant tumors \u2014 an important distinction when \"targeting p53\" is discussed."}

data: {"text": "[[10]]", "reference": {"citation_key": 10, "reference_text": "Duffy MJ, Synnott NC, O'Grady S, Crown J. <a target=\"_blank\" href=\"https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/32741700\">Targeting P53 for the Treatment of Cancer</a>. Seminars in Cancer Biology. 2022;79:58-67. doi:10.1016/j.semcancer.2020.07.005.", "reference_detail": {"title": "Targeting P53 for the Treatment of Cancer", "authors_string": "Duffy MJ, Synnott NC, O'Grady S, Crown J.", "publication_info_string": "Seminars in Cancer Biology. 2022;79:58-67. doi:10.1016/j.semcancer.2020.07.005.", "journal_name": "Seminars in Cancer Biology", "journal_short_name": "Semin Cancer Biol", "publication_date": "2022-02-01", "doi": "10.1016/j.semcancer.2020.07.005", "url": "https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/32741700"}, "source_texts": []}}

data: {"text": "[[32]]", "reference": {"citation_key": 32, "reference_text": "Al-Zoubi RM, Elaarag M, Zarour AA, et al. <a target=\"_blank\" href=\"https://doi.org/10.1002/ddr.70246\">Innovative Drug and Prodrug Candidates in Cancer Treatment Targeting TP53 Mutations: Challenge and Hope</a>. Drug Development Research. 2026;87(2):e70246. doi:10.1002/ddr.70246.", "reference_detail": {"title": "Innovative Drug and Prodrug Candidates in Cancer Treatment Targeting TP53 Mutations: Challenge and Hope", "authors_string": "Al-Zoubi RM, Elaarag M, Zarour AA, et al.", "publication_info_string": "Drug Development Research. 2026;87(2):e70246. doi:10.1002/ddr.70246.", "journal_name": "Drug Development Research", "journal_short_name": "Drug Dev Res", "publication_date": "2026-04-01", "doi": "10.1002/ddr.70246", "url": "https://doi.org/10.1002/ddr.70246"}, "source_texts": []}}

data: {"text": " At present, the pract"}

data: {"text": "ical guideline message remains that TP53 status should be assessed to inform prognosis and to select p53-independent regimens or trials, not because an approved TP53-directed drug exists."}

